xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/domain-cartridge-governance/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>ecos-test-cycle</name>\\n    <description>Edit→test→commit cycle for the ecos project. Run full test suite after code changes, verify results, commit on pass, recover on failure. Use whenever modifying ecos source code.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/ecos-test-cycle/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>external-agent-attach</name>\\n    <description>Attach an external AI agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, custom MCP host) to omostation via Agora MCP + BOS + agent-workflow. Use when onboarding a foreign agent, configuring MCP, or asking how to connect another agent to this workspace.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/external-agent-attach/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>git-discipline</name>\\n    <description>多 agent 并行下的 git 纪律：隔离工作树、交付三段式（add/commit/tag）、逃生口、子模块、僵尸锁、合并型交付补 claim、agent 自身 git 写能力自检。当你要提交代码、切换分支、碰子模块、做分支合并、遇到门禁拦截或 claim 冲突、或发现自己的文件消失 / git 行为诡异时使用。Triggers on: git commit, git merge, git checkout, 合并, 分支被切走, 文件消失, 提交丢了, claim 失败, 锁被占, index.lock, Operation not permitted, no-verify, 门禁拦截, D3, swarm-d3, submodule, 子模块, worktree, PASW, swarm-git, escape, unbound variable。</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/git-discipline/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>git-safety-check</name>\\n    <description>git 安全检查 skill：高危 git 操作（reset/push/子模块指针）前置校验与守门</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/git-safety-check/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>governance-phase-orchestrator</name>\\n    <description>Use when the user requests a governance-related task, P-phase closure, doc-lifecycle audit, frontmatter remediation, drift cleanup, or any workspace-wide convergence work. Triggers on keywords: 治理, 收敛, P 阶段, governance cycle, phase closure, drift, frontmatter, commit closure, linter saturation, 4 类分类, doc-lifecycle, RISE 循环.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/governance-phase-orchestrator/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>governance-ssot-edit</name>\\n    <description>Edit governance SSOT (governance-checks.yaml / gac-*.py / write-owners / x*-rules / mutation-surfaces) safely in a concurrent multi-agent workspace. Aligns ALL source copies, commits via pathspec to avoid clobbering concurrent staged work, pushes immediately so concurrent PRs can&apos;t silently revert, and verifies the change survives. Use when changing GaC rules/executor enums, governance registries, or any multi-source governance field.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/governance-ssot-edit/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>harness-compliance</name>\\n    <description>Harness 全生命周期合规检查 — 12 章节完整性 + MOF 约束联动 + OMO 状态同步</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/harness-compliance/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>kos-cold-start</name>\\n    <description>KOS 冷启动 skill：会话启动时从 KOS 加载 BRIEF/ADR/实体，对齐历史架构决策</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/kos-cold-start/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>memory-recall</name>\\n    <description>Unified memory recall/write routing for omostation agents (Memory OS). Use when searching knowledge, recalling user preferences, writing episodic memory, forgetting facts, or deciding between kos / gbrain / cards / inbox. Prefer bos://memory/mos/* (phase1+ live; phase10 as_of + optional live backends).\\n</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/memory-recall/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>multica-squad-ops</name>\\n    <description>用 multica CLI 落地日常工程协作 4 个 squad（交付流水线/架构评审/研究情报/运维监控）+ 配额动态分派台账。与 R3-executor 的 multica 后端物理隔离，不替代 ADR-0203 workflow。</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/multica-squad-ops/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>nextgen-cognitive-mesh</name>\\n    <description>Master governance skill for OMOStation Next-Gen Cognitive Mesh V3.0 (ADR-0200~0203). Guides memory self-distillation, cryptographic Merkle action ledgering, zero-config local edge compute roaming, and domain cartridge capsule packaging.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/nextgen-cognitive-mesh/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>omlxc-compute-fabric</name>\\n    <description>omlxc 异构算力织网、DFlash 2 块扩散投机解码、Radix 前缀树与 Paged KV 块内存、双区自适应量化与 75% 阶梯显存治理操作指南。当 Agent 需要执行本地大模型推理、预估长上下文显存、分析 Prompt 复杂度或调度本地算力时调用。</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/omlxc-compute-fabric/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>omo-audit-baseline</name>\\n    <description>Governance audit baseline workflow for the omostation workspace. Run omo audit, check results, commit governance data. Use when syncing governance state or running audit checks.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/omo-audit-baseline/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>project-governance</name>\\n    <description>Use when an agent changes this workspace or a child project and needs executable governance workflow routing instead of relying on AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md memory. ADR-0203 — all requirement iterations MUST start an agent-workflow run before edits.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/project-governance/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>round-gate-check</name>\\n    <description>回合门禁检查 skill：回合制执行的 gate 结果核验与放行判定</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/round-gate-check/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>round-workflow</name>\\n    <description>回合工作流 skill：回合制任务的状态机管理与轮次推进</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/round-workflow/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>scene-shadow-activate</name>\\n    <description>场景影子激活 skill：将 scene card 从 draft/shadow 阶段推进到 assisted/supervised 生命周期</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/scene-shadow-activate/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>spine-value-pipeline</name>\\n    <description>omostation (eCOS v6) 主干真值流与署名自进化技能包。指导 AI Agent 如何通过标准 bos:// 服务感知外部信号、驱动 Journey 状态机、调用本地主权算力生成草稿、在 Cockpit 呈递待办并捕获夏明星署名修改的 Diff 进行自适应学习。</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/spine-value-pipeline/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>swarm-escape</name>\\n    <description>蜂群逃生 skill：多 agent 冲突/死锁时的逃生阀与冲突升级路径</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/swarm-escape/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>system-index-distill</name>\\n    <description>Deep workspace analysis to find information silos and create unified navigation. Use when the workspace has many projects/SSOT sources and agents struggle to find things. Produces a SYSTEM-INDEX.md with pure pointers — no data duplication.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/system-index-distill/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>workflow-silence-detection</name>\\n    <description>Use when governance audits report silent workflows, P74 or p74_solidification warnings, compliance drift, or when planning workflow consolidation in the canonical split registry.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/workflow-silence-detection/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n  <skill>\\n    <name>worktree-ci-isolate</name>\\n    <description>Create isolated git worktrees for CI fixes and parallel development. Init submodules, work in isolation, clean up when done. Use when fixing CI issues or needing conflict-free parallel work.</description>\\n    <location>/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/.agents/skills/worktree-ci-isolate/SKILL.md</location>\\n  </skill>\\n</available_skills>\\n\\n<skills_usage>\\nThe `<description>` of each skill is a TRIGGER — it tells you *when* a skill applies. It is NOT a specification of what the skill does or how to do it. The procedure, scripts, commands, references, and required flags live only in the SKILL.md body. You do not know what a skill actually does until you have read its SKILL.md.\\n\\nMANDATORY activation flow:\\n1. Scan `<available_skills>` against the current user task.\\n2. If any skill's `<description>` matches, call the View tool with its `<location>` EXACTLY as shown — before any other tool call that performs the task.\\n3. Read the entire SKILL.md and follow its instructions.\\n4. Only then execute the task, using the skill's prescribed commands/tools.\\n\\nDo NOT skip step 2 because you think you already know how to do the task. Do NOT infer a skill's behavior from its name or description. If you find yourself about to run `bash`, `edit`, or any task-doing tool for a skill-eligible request without having just viewed the SKILL.md, stop and load the skill first.\\n\\nBuiltin skills (type=builtin) use virtual `crush://skills/...` location identifiers. The \\\"crush://\\\" prefix is NOT a URL, network address, or MCP resource — it is a special internal identifier the View tool understands natively. Pass the `<location>` verbatim to View.\\n\\nDo not use MCP tools (including read_mcp_resource) to load skills.\\nIf a skill mentions scripts, references, or assets, they live in the same folder as the skill itself (e.g., scripts/, references/, assets/ subdirectories within the skill's folder).\\n</skills_usage>\\n\\n\\n\\n# Project-Specific Context\\nMake sure to follow the instructions in the context below.\\n<project_context>\\n\\n<file path=\\\"/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/AGENTS.md\\\">\\n---\\ntype: ssot\\nowner: governance-team\\nlast_updated: 2026-09-04\\n---\\n\\n# AGENTS.md — Workspace Development Guide\\n\\n> Root operating guide for AI coding agents. **Keep operational** — runtime facts go in SSOT files, not here.\\n\\n## 0. Worktree Policy (Mandatory)\\n\\n> **Main workspace is read-only. Every new change starts from an isolated worktree.**\\n\\n| Action | Required |\\n|--------|----------|\\n| New feature / fix / cleanup | `bash bin/gac/gac-worktree.sh claim <session>` |\\n| Direct commit to main | ❌ Prohibited |\\n\\n**Full policy**: [`GOVERNANCE.md`](GOVERNANCE.md) § Worktree Isolation\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Read This First (Before Every Edit)\\n\\n1. Read [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md) for session startup context.\\n2. Read the target project `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`.\\n3. Check `git status --short`.\\n4. **需求迭代强制 Workflow（ADR-0203）** — Run `bootstrap → start --profile → claim` before any requirement delivery edit. Use `bin/agent-workflow.py compliance` for compliance audit.\\n5. For governed state, use OMO/C2G brokers instead of direct `.omo` writes.\\n6. For multi-file or high-risk changes, explain the edit surface before applying patches.\\n7. All local/edge LLM inference MUST route through **AetherForge (`bos://compute/aetherforge/infer`)**.\\n\\n### Key SSOT Registries\\n\\n| Registry | Purpose |\\n|----------|---------|\\n| `.omo/_truth/registry/agent-workflows/` | Agent workflow facts |\\n| `.omo/_truth/registry/ci-surfaces.yaml` | CI 平面检查接线 |\\n| `.omo/_truth/registry/runtime-projections.yaml` | Runtime projections |\\n| `.omo/_truth/registry/governance-checks.yaml` | GaC rules |\\n| `docs/project-registry.yaml` | Project metadata |\\n\\n### Governance Quick Reference\\n\\n| Need | Command |\\n|------|---------|\\n| MOF constraint check | `ecos-constraint explain/audit/eval/drift` |\\n| Domain truth hygiene | `make hygiene-patrol` |\\n| Policy-as-code | `ecos-constraint policy audit/explain/list` |\\n| Intent-to-spec | `ecos-constraint intent compile` |\\n| Shadow challenge | `ecos-constraint challenge [--auto-patch]` |\\n| Sovereign compute | `omlxc fabric snapshot` |\\n| Cartridge factory | `ecos-constraint cartridge list/export/validate` |\\n\\n**Binding architecture (DFSQ/SFOP)**: Mesh (`COMP-WS-omo`) is the only active `S` slot. Do **not** add a second dispatcher or fifth ontology.\\n\\n### 能力发现\\n\\n| 需求 | 入口 |\\n|------|------|\\n| 查看所有可用 skills | `cat .agents/skills/INDEX.md`（按域分组，由 generator 派生; 运行 `find .agents/skills -name SKILL.md | wc -l` 取实时计数） |\\n| 查看所有 workflows | `cat .omo/_truth/registry/agent-workflows/INDEX.md`（按 generator 派生; 运行 `find .omo/_truth/registry/agent-workflows -name \\\"*.yaml\\\" | wc -l` 取实时计数） |\\n| 智能推荐 workflow | `uv run python bin/agent-workflow.py suggest --from-diff --profile <agent>` |\\n| Cockpit CLI 命令 | `cockpit <domain> <verb>`（详见 `docs/CLI-REFERENCE.md`） |\\n| BOS 服务发现 | `.omo/_truth/registry/capability-providers.yaml` |\\n| MCP 工具清单 | `docs/generated/capability-registry.yaml` |\\n| MCP/BOS URI 完整性 | `python3 bin/gac/check-mcp-bos-uri-completeness.py`（`--warn` 模式审计不阻断） |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Documentation SSOT Contract\\n\\n| Document | Owns |\\n|----------|------|\\n| `README.md` | Front door and quick orientation |\\n| `CLAUDE.md` | AI session startup protocol |\\n| `AGENTS.md` | Workspace operating rules |\\n| `ARCHITECTURE.md` | Stable architecture contracts |\\n| `docs/project-registry.yaml` | Project metadata facts |\\n| `.omo/_truth/registry/governance-checks.yaml` | GaC rules |\\n\\n**Do not hard-code** current phase, health score, test counts, or port values in Markdown. Use pointers.\\n\\n**文档归档约定**（T6-17 治理，2026-09-05）：`type: ephemeral + status: completed` 的一次性文档（总结/交接/审计报告）完成后归档到 `.omo/_knowledge/design/plans/archive/`（`.omo/_archive/` 被 .gitignore 忽略，新文件不可用），顶层不再留存；文档引用同步改为归档路径（指针化）。SSOT 判定盘点见 `docs/reports/doc-ssot-inventory-2026-09-05.md`。\\n\\nFull contract: [`.omo/standards/doc-ssot-contract.md`](.omo/standards/doc-ssot-contract.md)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Architecture Summary\\n\\nStable architecture contracts: [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](ARCHITECTURE.md)\\nProject layer placement: [`docs/generated/project-layer-index.md`](docs/generated/project-layer-index.md)\\n\\n**道法术器 (DFSQ/v1)**: `python3 bin/gac/check-sfop-slots.py --json`\\n**Execution chain**: `python3 bin/gac/check-execution-chain.py --json`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Governance Boundaries\\n\\n| Surface | Rule |\\n|---------|------|\\n| `.omo/` | State/evidence plane. Do not add long-lived execution logic. |\\n| `projects/omo/` | Governance kernel: schema, audit, sync, broker, lint. |\\n| `projects/ecos/` | Protocol and MOF layer. |\\n| `bin/` | Governance tools. Do not edit runtime state manually. |\\n| `config/` | Machine identity. Do not edit manually. |\\n| `kos/` | Knowledge index. Runtime product, do not edit manually. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Essential Commands\\n\\n### Agent Workflow (single entry)\\n\\n```bash\\nuv run --with \\\"pyyaml\\\" python \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" bootstrap\\nuv run --with \\\"pyyaml\\\" python \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" compliance\\nuv run --with \\\"pyyaml\\\" python \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" start <workflow-id> --profile <agent-profile> --bet <BET-ID> --objective \\\"<summary>\\\"\\nuv run --with \\\"pyyaml\\\" python \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" claim <run-id> --path <path>\\nuv run --with \\\"pyyaml\\\" python \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" closeout <run-id>\\n```\\n\\n### Gates & Lint\\n\\n```bash\\nmake gac-local-gate          # Full local governance gate\\nmake ci-local                # All local CI checks\\npython3 bin/gac/ci-check-runner.py --workflow governance-check.yml\\n```\\n\\n### Testing\\n\\n```bash\\nbash \\\"tests/integration/run-all.sh\\\"    # Root integration suite\\ncd \\\"projects/knowledge/kairon\\\" && make test-diff\\ncd \\\"projects/knowledge/gbrain\\\" && bun test\\n```\\n\\n### SSOT & State\\n\\n```bash\\nmake ssot-guardian && make ssot-sync\\npython3 bin/gac/meta-doctor.py --workspace . --json\\n```\\n\\n**Full catalog**: [`bin/README.md`](bin/README.md) | **CLI reference**: [`docs/CLI-REFERENCE.md`](docs/CLI-REFERENCE.md)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Git And Submodules\\n\\n- Do not run `git commit`, `git push`, `git reset --hard`, or branch switching unless explicitly asked.\\n- **Submodule pointer update**: `bash bin/ssot/submodule-pointer-transaction.sh --message \\\"...\\\"`.\\n- **禁止 `sed -i` 做添加/删除条目操作** — use Python `read → check → modify → write`.\\n- **子模块 commit 三步走**: ① `cd projects/<sub> && git add && git commit` ② `git push` (子模块内) ③ `cd 主仓 && git add projects/<sub> && git commit && push`.\\n- **pull --rebase 风险**: 本地 commit 基于旧 main 时可能丢弃改动。rebase 后用 `git reflog` 确认。\\n\\n### 高危 git 操作守门\\n\\n- **`reset --hard` 前三确认**: ① 当前分支 ② reset 目标 = 该分支的 origin 状态 ③ 工作树干净。\\n- **改\\\"看起来是子项目\\\"的代码前确认仓库边界**: `ls -d <path>/.git` + `git -C <path> remote -v`.\\n\\n### PR 工作流\\n\\n```bash\\nbash bin/gac/gac-worktree.sh claim <session>   # 起隔离 worktree\\nbash bin/gac/gac-worktree.sh submit <session>   # push 分支 + 开 PR\\nbash bin/gac/gac-worktree.sh merge <session>    # squash 合并 PR\\n```\\n\\n### Hook 机制 22c（2026-09-06, BET-Y1Q4-T6-24）\\n\\n- **本仓 `core.hooksPath=.githooks`**：hooks 从 canonical 直读生效。`git rev-parse --git-path hooks` 会被重定向到 `.githooks`（不是真实 git-dir/hooks）。\\n- **元数据路径纪律**：installer/runner/health-check 写读 `.version`/`.content-hash` 一律用 `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/hooks`（worktree 感知、不受 hooksPath 影响）；**不要用 `--git-dir`**（worktree 下返回 `.git/worktrees/<name>/`，读不到共享元数据 → 版本误报 0.0.0，2026-09-06 实证）；也不用 `--git-path hooks`（core.hooksPath 下 cp 自拷贝/检查错位，2026-09-06 实证回归）。\\n- **manifest 引用路径全量扫描**：改 hook 脚本路径后必须扫描 manifest 全部 hook 段（pre-commit/pre-push/post-checkout/pre-rebase/pre-merge-commit/post-merge/commit-msg），别只修一段——#3282 只改 pre-commit 段、回退 pre-merge-commit 的 conflict-marker 路径致检查静默失效。\\n- **同 BET 并行交付防回退**：改 canonical hooks 前先 `git fetch` 查 main 是否已含目标内容（PITFALL-GAT-006）；并行 agent 同名 BET 的 PR 可能基于旧 main、合并后回退正确值（#3282 回退 #3277 的 5 处修复实录）。\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Testing Guidance\\n\\n| Change Surface | Minimum Verification |\\n|----------------|----------------------|\\n| Documentation only | `make gac-local-gate` and diff review |\\n| Python code | Targeted `uv run pytest` |\\n| kairon | `make test-diff` from `projects/knowledge/kairon` |\\n| gbrain | `bun test` |\\n| Cross-project | Targeted tests on every touched consumer |\\n\\nIf a test cannot run, report why and what risk remains.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Closeout Checklist\\n\\n1. Review `git diff --stat`.\\n2. Run the verification appropriate for the change.\\n3. Prefer `make agent-workflow-closeout RUN_ID=<run-id>` for governed runs.\\n4. Mention files changed and checks run.\\n5. Do not create commits unless explicitly requested and confirmed.\\n6. **大任务后复盘+固化**: 教训写 memory + AGENTS.md (协议层) + hook (harness 层).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Architecture Standards (Agent 必读)\\n\\n**场景卡生命周期** (5 级): `draft → shadow → assisted → supervised → routine`\\n- 标准: `.omo/standards/scene-card-lifecycle.yaml`\\n- 升级必须按顺序，shadow 需 3-sample，assisted 需 30-sample + calibration ≥ 0.6\\n\\n**业务域** (5 域): `work` / `health` / `research` / `knowledge` / `governance`\\n- 标准: `.omo/standards/business-domains.yaml`\\n\\n**维度系统** (12 维度): 治理维 4 + 业务维 7 + 新增维 1\\n- 标准: `.omo/standards/dimension-system.yaml`\\n\\n**价值循环** (5 阶段): 信号感知 → 信号分类 → 旅程执行 → 价值记录 → 进化反馈\\n- 标准: `.omo/standards/value-loop-standard.yaml`\\n\\n**架构校验**: `make architecture-check`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Harness 集成 (Phase 8)\\n\\n- **Cockpit CLI**: `cockpit harness <command>` (12 子命令)\\n- **8 阶段 DAG**: `admission → spec → grill → dispatch → execute → verify → audit → accept`\\n- **Hook 层**: 6 个 exit 1 拦截点 (pre-commit)\\n- **GaC 规则**: 32 个强制/高优先级规则\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 bin/gac/harness-compliance-check.py --report\\ncockpit harness compliance|full|status\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Key Patterns & References\\n\\n- **Historical patterns**: `.omo/_knowledge/patterns/` (P75, P91, P43, P71, P72, P78, etc.)\\n- **分支等价性判据**: 只用 **内容 diff** (`git diff origin/main...<branch>`)\\n- **动手前先查 main 是否已自愈 (PITFALL-GAT-006)**: claim/start 前先 `git fetch origin main` 并做内容等价检查 — 被改文件在最新 main 是否已含目标内容 (`git diff origin/main...<branch>` 是否为空/仅剩预期增量), `git log --oneline origin/main -N` 是否已有同类 PR. 多 agent 并发下修复目标可能已被其他 PR 达成 (total_bets #3099 / scene-cards #3097 两次复发); 已合入则放弃分支, 勿开 PR — 否则 PR 合并会回退 main 正确值.\\n- **Resident Agent**: `make resident-status` | BOS: `bos://resident/*`\\n- **BCOS**: `make bcos-evolve` | `python3 bin/bc-os/evolution_engine.py --json`\\n- **ADR index**: `.omo/_knowledge/decisions/`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. 归档/收敛项目说明\\n\\n- agora-dashboard 独立入口已收敛 (能力并入 cockpit/agora)\\n- (归档) hermes-console 与 dashboard_server 作为子应用挂载 (L3 入口能力收敛到 cockpit/agora)\\n\\n</file>\\n\\n<file path=\\\"/Users/xiamingxing/Workspace/CLAUDE.md\\\">\\n---\\ntype: ssot\\nowner: governance-team\\nlast_updated: 2026-09-03\\n---\\n\\n# CLAUDE.md — omostation AI Context Loader\\n\\n> 最后更新: 2026-09-03\\n> Purpose: session startup protocol for AI agents.\\n> Detailed engineering rules live in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md).\\n> Stable architecture contracts live in [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](ARCHITECTURE.md).\\n> Document ownership is governed by [`.omo/standards/doc-ssot-contract.md`](.omo/standards/doc-ssot-contract.md).\\n\\n## 0. This Repo At A Glance\\n\\n`omostation` is the root workspace for **eCOS v6**: a multi-project workspace for knowledge engineering, agent governance, BOS service routing, runtime orchestration, and personal/work knowledge operations.\\n\\n- **Shape**: a polyglot monorepo. Sub-projects live under `projects/*` and are mostly independent git submodules — Python via `uv`, TypeScript via `bun`, plus Docker. Each sub-project has its own `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` and may expose project-local build commands; read its guidance before editing.\\n- **Architecture skeleton** (concepts only — full contracts in [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](ARCHITECTURE.md)): the `5+4+1+1` layering (L0 protocol → L1 runtime → L2 kernel → L3 entry → L4 docs), the `X1-X4` governance axes, and BOS URI domain routing. Binding runtime grammar is **道法术器 (DFSQ)** nested on MOF plus **脊面运行模式 (SFOP)** slots — [`docs/architecture/dao-fa-shu-qi.md`](docs/architecture/dao-fa-shu-qi.md) and [`docs/architecture/os-operating-pattern-v1.md`](docs/architecture/os-operating-pattern-v1.md). Agents must obey slot grammar (unique Mesh dispatcher, no parallel OS) rather than adding AGE-v2/resident/BCOS as a second control plane. Layer/project placement → [`docs/generated/project-layer-index.md`](docs/generated/project-layer-index.md); BOS domains → ARCHITECTURE.md §4; entry surfaces → ARCHITECTURE.md §3.\\n- **Document division of labor** (orthogonal SSOT — each doc owns one dimension):\\n\\n  - runtime facts → machine-readable SSOT (`.omo/state/system.yaml`, `docs/project-registry.yaml`, `protocols/*-registry.yaml`)\\n  - stable architecture → [`ARCHITECTURE.md`](ARCHITECTURE.md) / [`LAYER-INDEX.md`](LAYER-INDEX.md)\\n  - operating rules → [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) + this file\\n  - front-door entry → [`README.md`](README.md)\\n  - **system navigation** → [`docs/SYSTEM-INDEX.md`](docs/SYSTEM-INDEX.md) (NEW: unified navigation hub)\\n  - **agent capabilities & board consensus** → [`.agents/skills/bdsk-virtual-board/SKILL.md`](.agents/skills/bdsk-virtual-board/SKILL.md) (B.D.S.K. Mode-A/B 4-Corner debate matrix & AetherForge/omlxc local compute architecture)\\n\\n> **First Stop**: Read [`docs/SYSTEM-INDEX.md`](docs/SYSTEM-INDEX.md) to understand the workspace structure, then use the specialized indexes:\\n>\\n> - [`docs/INDEX-PROJECTS.md`](docs/INDEX-PROJECTS.md) — find projects by layer/stack\\n> - [`docs/INDEX-TOOLS.md`](docs/INDEX-TOOLS.md) — find tools and scripts\\n> - [`docs/INDEX-KNOWLEDGE.md`](docs/INDEX-KNOWLEDGE.md) — find ADRs, audits, patterns\\n> - [`docs/INDEX-AGENTS.md`](docs/INDEX-AGENTS.md) — find skills and agent setup\\n>\\n> **This file is a navigation layer only.** It does not duplicate project counts, ports, service inventories, test counts, phase, health scores, layer tables, or rule registries. Hard-coding those violates `doc-ssot-contract` and fails `bin/ssot/doc-ssot-lint.py`.\\n\\n## 1. Startup Protocol\\n\\nLoad context before changing code or governed state. Two phases — run Step A when you need to align your mental model with historical decisions; run Step B before every editing session.\\n\\n### Step A · Situational load (KOS cold-start — first turn, or when realigning to architecture)\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> **KOS (Knowledge Operating System) Hardware Cold-Start Protocol**\\n> You are equipped with `mcp-server-kos` as your external read-only hard drive.\\n> To align your mental model and avoid historical architectural regressions, run this KOS query sequence:\\n>\\n> 1. **Query Current Decisions & Goals**:\\n>    `mcp-server-kos::query_custom_sql(sql=\\\"SELECT doc_id, title, canonical_path FROM documents WHERE canonical_path LIKE '%BRIEF.md%' LIMIT 1\\\")`\\n>    Read the resulting BRIEF.md path. It carries active technical debts (needs-human) and X3 metrics.\\n> 2. **Traverse ADR Decisions**:\\n>    `mcp-server-kos::search_kos(query=\\\"ADR-012\\\")`\\n>    Pay attention to ADR-0124 (S1 retrospective) and ADR-0125 (S2 retrospective).\\n> 3. **Identify Domain Schemas**:\\n>    `mcp-server-kos::list_entities(limit=50)`\\n\\n### Step B · Workflow load (every editing session)\\n\\n```bash\\nmake agent-workflow-bootstrap\\nmake agent-workflow-status\\n```\\n\\nRead the SSOT files reported by `bootstrap` for task-specific runtime facts — **do not copy their values into this document** (they drift quickly). If MCP context is available, prefer the cockpit `workspace_context` tool.\\n\\n### Step B.0 · 全局状态快速感知 (Multi-Agent Swarm Status)\\n\\n在开工或排查前，先运行状态快照：\\n\\n```bash\\nmake omo-status        # 或 bin/omo-status：<0.2s 秒级 Rich 快照 (Agent心跳/锁/子仓/BET)\\nmake omo-top           # 或 bin/omo-top：Textual 实时 4 象限互动大盘\\n```\\n\\n**Agent Session Dashboard（ASD）**：会话冷启动信息聚合规格见\\n[`docs/plans/2026-09-06-agent-session-dashboard-spec.md`](docs/plans/2026-09-06-agent-session-dashboard-spec.md)\\n（`BET-Y1Q4-T9-03`）。MVP CLI（`bin/agent-session-dashboard.py`）由后续 `T9-04` 交付；在此之前用\\n`omo-status` + `bet-ledger status` + bootstrap 组合代替。\\n\\n### Step B.0.5 · 架构约束检查 (每次编辑会话)\\n\\n编辑架构相关文件前，必须检查以下约束:\\n\\n1. **场景卡生命周期**: 必须按 draft→shadow→assisted→supervised→routine 顺序升级\\n2. **业务域分类**: 每个场景卡必须有 domain 字段 (work/health/research/knowledge/governance)\\n3. **脚本配额**: 新增 bin/ 脚本必须同步归档旧脚本 (add 1 = delete 1)\\n4. **SSOT 引用**: 优先引用 `.omo/standards/` 下的标准文件，不要硬编码运行时值\\n\\n### Step B.1 · 需求迭代强制 Workflow（ADR-0203）\\n\\n所有需求迭代必须先 `start` 再改文件。详见 [`AGENTS.md` §1.1](AGENTS.md)。\\n\\n### Step B.2 · 三年规划执行台账\\n\\n不确定当前该做哪件事时，读台账，不要自行拟定任务。详见 [`AGENTS.md` §1.4](AGENTS.md)。\\n\\n### Step B.3 · 多 Agent 并行的 Git 纪律\\n\\n共享主树上并行的 agent 会互相删除产物。详见 [`AGENTS.md` §1.3](AGENTS.md) · skill `git-discipline`。\\n\\n## 1.5 P74 Workflow Solidification Check (ADR-0130)\\n\\nAfter bootstrap, every agent MUST verify P74 health. P74 is the常态化 mechanism\\n(常态化机制) for agent-workflow silence detection — see `.omo/_knowledge/decisions/0130-p74-workflow-solidification.md`.\\n\\n```bash\\nmake agent-workflow-compliance\\n```\\n\\nRead `.p74_solidification.warn_count`:\\n\\n- `0`: continue\\n- `> 0` (any silent workflow counts; `handoff-resume` and `observer-audit` no longer\\n  excluded per ADR-0211 §D1): treat as governance signal.\\n  Read `.omo/standards/p74-solidification-contract.md` §3 decision tree for actions.\\n  If workflow has neither `has_recent_run` nor `has_check_coverage`, register it via\\n  `agent-workflows/::diff_checks`. Extending `silent_workflow_policy.excluded_workflows`\\n  is no longer supported (field removed in ADR-0211 §D1).\\n\\nThe `silent_workflow_policy` field in `agent-workflows/` is the SSOT for\\nsilent workflow classification. Per-workflow `run_frequency` field (on_demand /\\nperiodic / continuous) drives the warn_after threshold (30d / 7d / 1d).\\n\\n## 2. Session Role\\n\\n`CLAUDE.md` is the lightweight context loader. It answers only:\\n\\n- What must be read first?\\n- Which files are authoritative?\\n- Which operations are unsafe without a broker or explicit user request?\\n- Where is deeper guidance found?\\n\\nIt must not duplicate project tables, architecture diagrams, historical closeout reports, rule registries, test counts, port values, or generated snapshots.\\n\\n## 3. Mandatory Boundaries\\n\\nThe authoritative SSOT map (all fact types, sources, and boundaries) lives in [`ARCHITECTURE.md` §1](ARCHITECTURE.md). Read it before hard-coding any runtime fact, port, vault path, or governed-state write.\\n\\n## 4. Working Discipline\\n\\n1. For work with more than a couple of steps, keep a visible todo list.\\n2. Read the target project `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` before editing that project.\\n3. Use `rg` for text discovery; for callers/impact prefer codebase-memory MCP (see [`.omo/_archive/operations-2026H1/codebase-memory.md`](.omo/_archive/operations-2026H1/codebase-memory.md)).\\n4. Use the available file-editing tools (Edit, Create, MultiEdit, or `apply_patch`) for manual edits.\\n5. Do not delete, reset, move, commit, or push unless explicitly confirmed. See [`AGENTS.md` §6](AGENTS.md#6-git-and-submodules) for the full git and submodule policy.\\n6. If a governance protocol demands a commit but the current user/session policy does not authorize one, finish the working-tree changes, report the exact files, and ask for explicit commit confirmation.\\n\\n## 5. Common Commands\\n\\n<!-- doc-ssot-lint: raw form \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" bootstrap, \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" closeout, \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" compliance -->\\n\\n```bash\\nuv run --with \\\"pyyaml\\\" python \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" bootstrap   # 单入口: 加载 SSOT 运行时事实\\nuv run --with \\\"pyyaml\\\" python \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" closeout <run-id>   # 闭环收尾\\nuv run --with \\\"pyyaml\\\" python \\\"bin/agent-workflow.py\\\" compliance  # 合规审计\\n```\\n\\nFor the full command reference (gate & lint, SSOT tracking, agent workflow lifecycle, state sync, scene cards & journeys, tests), see [`AGENTS.md` §5](AGENTS.md).\\n\\n## 6. Routing Hints\\n\\nThe authoritative SSOT map (fact types → sources) lives in [`ARCHITECTURE.md` §1](ARCHITECTURE.md). Use the INDEX docs to narrow by category:\\n\\n| Need | Route |\\n|------|-------|\\n| Projects by layer/stack | [`docs/INDEX-PROJECTS.md`](docs/INDEX-PROJECTS.md) |\\n| Tools and scripts | [`docs/INDEX-TOOLS.md`](docs/INDEX-TOOLS.md) |\\n| ADRs, audits, patterns | [`docs/INDEX-KNOWLEDGE.md`](docs/INDEX-KNOWLEDGE.md) |\\n| Agent skills & setup | [`docs/INDEX-AGENTS.md`](docs/INDEX-AGENTS.md) |\\n| System navigation hub | [`docs/SYSTEM-INDEX.md`](docs/SYSTEM-INDEX.md) |\\n| Scene cards & journeys | [`docs/scene-cards/`](docs/scene-cards/) · [`docs/journey-specs/`](docs/journey-specs/) |\\n| Code callers / impact | [`.omo/_archive/operations-2026H1/codebase-memory.md`](.omo/_archive/operations-2026H1/codebase-memory.md) |\\n\\nFor task-level routing (BOS, governance, ports, ADRs, main landing, scene admission), see [`ARCHITECTURE.md` §1](ARCHITECTURE.md) and the INDEX docs above.\\n\\n## 6.5 Anti-Corrosion Five-Layer Framework (ADR-0431)\\n\\nRules carry lifecycles (`added_at`/`review_before`/`justification` in `governance-checks.yaml::gac.rules`). Check health: `python3 bin/gac/rules-lifecycle.py` (weekly cron; expired → subtraction candidates). Human authority layers L1-L5 (charter/context/decision/constraints/unknown) are orthogonal — see `.omo/_knowledge/decisions/0431-anti-corrosion-five-layer-framework.md`. BOS: `bos://governance/anti-corrosion/*`. MCP: `rules_lifecycle` tool.\\n\\n\\n## 7. Closeout\\n\\n```bash\\ngit status --short\\nmake gac-local-gate\\nmake ssot-guardian\\nmake scene-card-check    # scene card 变更时\\nmake journey-check       # journey spec 变更时\\nmake adr-number-check    # ADR 变更时\\n```\\n\\nRun broader tests only when the edited surface warrants them. Documentation-only changes usually need the documentation SSOT check plus a clear diff review. For the full closeout checklist (including reporting files changed and checks skipped), see [`AGENTS.md` §9](AGENTS.md#9-closeout-checklist).\\n\\n## 🧬 Onboarding Consensus (🧬 历史演进避坑基因)\\n\\n> **自动刷新时间**: 2026-07-06 15:44:53 | 模式: RAG Top-2 按需激活\\n> 新进 Agent 必须通读并深度对齐以下前人沉淀的历史避坑基因，严禁在同一坑中二次栽倒：\\n\\n- **P74 — Workflow Solidification Pattern (常态化工作流沉默治理)** ([p74-workflow-solidification-pattern.md](.omo/_knowledge/patterns/p74-workflow-solidification-pattern.md))\\n  > 任一即触发 P74 评估: 1. **沉默 workflow**:registry 登记 ≥ 1 周,无 `agent_workflow_start` 事件。 2. **错位 workflow**:实际做的事 ≥ 3 次,却走通用 `project-code-change` 而非专属 workflow。\\n\\n- **P73 Truth-Driven Engineering Pattern — eCOS 多迁移/并发/声明执行鸿沟下的工程纪律** ([p73-truth-driven-engineering-pattern.md](.omo/_knowledge/patterns/p73-truth-driven-engineering-pattern.md))\\n  > | 陷阱 | 症状 | 本轮案例 | |------|------|---------| | **D1** 凭路径直觉判存在性 | 报\\\"X 零实现/不存在/悬空\\\" 其实文件已迁移或运行时写面未创建 | 连续 3 轮把 debt(空=运行时写面正常) / task(卡 ingress delivery) / GaC(3 drift 非 129) 判错 |\\n\\n## 治理活性自检 (2026-08-22 自进化框架)\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 bin/gac/meta-doctor.py --workspace . --json   # 治理活性巡检\\npython3 bin/scheduler-compile.py --check               # 调度一致性\\n```\\n\\n## Resident Agent 体系 (2026-08-23, WP-A~I / ADR-0396)\\n\\n事件驱动常驻 agent 运行时：五类角色（sediment/decision/execute/monitor/heartbeat）+ 规则级路由订阅。详见 [`docs/architecture/resident-agent-system-v1.md`](docs/architecture/resident-agent-system-v1.md)。\\n\\n```bash\\nmake resident-status       # 运行状态快照 (daemon/events/sediment/alert/ledger)\\nmake resident-roles        # 五类角色配置\\nmake resident-daemon       # 单次 tick 调试\\n```\\n\\n- 路由表 SSOT: `projects/omo/src/omo/resident/resident-routes.yaml`\\n- 角色 SSOT: `omo resident roles`（`projects/omo/src/omo/resident/roles.py`）\\n- MOF: `mof/m2/digital_agent.yaml`（DigitalAgent, tier=resident）· BOS: `bos://resident/*`\\n- agora MCP: `resident_status` / `resident_roles`（`projects/agora/src/agora/server/tools_resident.py`，委派 `omo resident status/roles`）\\n\\n## BCOS 业务域系统 (2026-08-23, W1~W4)\\n\\n业务闭环系统：信号路由 → 进化引擎 → 北极星价值度量。详见 [`docs/architecture/bcos-system-v1.md`](docs/architecture/bcos-system-v1.md)。\\n\\n```bash\\nmake bcos-evolve       # 进化引擎四阶段 (observe/propose/evaluate/approve, dry-run 默认)\\nmake bcos-signals      # 统一信号路由 (W1-D2)\\nmake bcos-north-star   # 北极星价值度量 v2\\n```\\n\\n- 进化引擎: `bin/bc-os/evolution_engine.py`（EvolutionEngine 四阶段）\\n- 信号路由: `bin/bc-os/signal_router.py`（W1-D2, 公文/会议/调研/代码）\\n- 北极星: `bin/bc-os/north_star_meter_v2.py`（排除 self-data）\\n- MOF: `mof/m2/bcos_system.yaml`（BCOSystem）· BOS: `bos://bcos/*`\\n\\n</file>\\n\\n</project_context>\\n\\n\\n\",\n      \"role\": \"system\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"content\": \"<system_reminder>This is a reminder that your todo list is currently empty. DO NOT mention this to the user explicitly because they are already aware.\\nIf you are working on tasks that would benefit from a todo list please use the \\\"todos\\\" tool to create one.\\nIf not, please feel free to ignore. Again do not mention this message to the user.</system_reminder>\",\n      \"role\": \"user\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"content\": \"hi\",\n      \"role\": \"user\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"model\": \"vision\",\n  \"max_tokens\": 2048,\n  \"stream_options\": {\n    \"include_usage\": true\n  },\n  \"tool_choice\": \"auto\",\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"agent\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Launch a new agent that has access to the following tools: glob, grep, ls, view. When you are searching for a keyword or file and are not confident that you will find the right match on the first try, use the agent tool to perform the search for you.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"The task for the agent to perform\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"agentic_fetch\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Fetch a URL or search the web using an AI sub-agent that can extract, summarize, and answer questions. Slower and costlier than fetch; use fetch for raw content or API responses.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"The prompt describing what information to find or extract\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"url\": {\n              \"description\": \"The URL to fetch content from (optional - if not provided, the agent will search the web)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"bash\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Execute shell commands; long-running commands automatically move to background and return a shell ID.\\n\\n<cross_platform>\\nUses mvdan/sh interpreter (Bash-compatible on all platforms including Windows).\\nUse forward slashes for paths: \\\"ls C:/foo/bar\\\" not \\\"ls C:\\\\foo\\\\bar\\\".\\nCommon shell builtins and core utils available on Windows.\\n</cross_platform>\\n\\n<execution_steps>\\n1. Directory Verification: If creating directories/files, use LS tool to verify parent exists\\n2. Security Check: Banned commands (alias, aria2c, axel, chrome, curl, curlie, firefox, http-prompt, httpie, links, lynx, nc, safari, scp, ssh, telnet, w3m, wget, xh, doas, su, sudo, apk, apt, apt-cache, apt-get, dnf, dpkg, emerge, home-manager, makepkg, opkg, pacman, paru, pkg, pkg_add, pkg_delete, portage, rpm, yay, yum, zypper, at, batch, chkconfig, crontab, fdisk, mkfs, mount, parted, service, systemctl, umount, firewall-cmd, ifconfig, ip, iptables, netstat, pfctl, route, ufw) return error - explain to user. Safe read-only commands execute without prompts\\n3. Command Execution: Execute with proper quoting, capture output\\n4. Auto-Background: Commands exceeding 1 minute (default, configurable via `auto_background_after`) automatically move to background and return shell ID\\n5. Output Processing: Truncate if exceeds 30000 characters\\n6. Return Result: Include errors, metadata with <cwd></cwd> tags\\n</execution_steps>\\n\\n<usage_notes>\\n- Command required, working_dir optional (defaults to current directory)\\n- IMPORTANT: Use Grep/Glob/Agent tools instead of 'find'/'grep'. Use View/LS tools instead of 'cat'/'head'/'tail'/'ls'\\n- Chain with ';' or '&&', avoid newlines except in quoted strings\\n- Each command runs in independent shell (no state persistence between calls)\\n- Prefer absolute paths over 'cd' (use 'cd' only if user explicitly requests)\\n- Ripgrep (`rg`) is available; prefer it over `grep` for faster, more intuitive searching\\n</usage_notes>\\n\\n<background_execution>\\n- Set run_in_background=true to run commands in a separate background shell\\n- Returns a shell ID for managing the background process\\n- Use job_output tool to view current output from background shell\\n- Use job_kill tool to terminate a background shell\\n- IMPORTANT: NEVER use `&` at the end of commands to run in background - use run_in_background parameter instead\\n- Commands that should run in background:\\n  * Long-running servers (e.g., `npm start`, `python -m http.server`, `node server.js`)\\n  * Watch/monitoring tasks (e.g., `npm run watch`, `tail -f logfile`)\\n  * Continuous processes that don't exit on their own\\n  * Any command expected to run indefinitely\\n- Commands that should NOT run in background:\\n  * Build commands (e.g., `npm run build`, `go build`)\\n  * Test suites (e.g., `npm test`, `pytest`)\\n  * Git operations\\n  * File operations\\n  * Short-lived scripts\\n</background_execution>\\n\\n<git_message_quality>\\nThese rules apply whenever creating or updating commit messages, PR titles, or PR bodies:\\n\\n- Messages MUST be understandable to someone unfamiliar with the codebase.\\n- Before creating or updating a message, verify this litmus test: a new contributor reading only the commit message or PR title/body should understand what problem this solves, why it matters, and the impact without opening files, reading the diff, or knowing internal code names.\\n- Avoid code identifiers, filenames, function names, and implementation details unless they are necessary for understanding the user-facing impact.\\n- Bad: \\\"Add NameFromHex with sync.Once lazy init\\\"\\n- Good: \\\"Improve color name lookup performance while keeping startup fast\\\"\\n</git_message_quality>\\n\\n<commit_messages>\\nCommit messages are for future readers scanning history. Before committing:\\n\\n- Follow <git_message_quality>.\\n- Draft a concise 1-2 sentence message focusing on why the change exists and what outcome it enables, not a list of files or implementation details.\\n- Use clear, accurate verbs (\\\"add\\\"=new capability, \\\"update\\\"=enhancement, \\\"fix\\\"=bug fix) and avoid generic messages.\\n- The first line MUST be under 72 characters.\\n- Add a body only when it is needed to explain the reasoning, tradeoffs, or important context; wrap body lines at 72 characters.\\n- If the change is internal-only, still describe the benefit or maintenance outcome rather than naming private code.\\n- Bad: \\\"fix: nil pointer in session.go\\\"\\n- Good: \\\"fix: prevent session loading from crashing on missing metadata\\\"\\n- Bad: \\\"refactor: move PromptBuilder into internal/agent\\\"\\n- Good: \\\"refactor: make prompt assembly easier to maintain\\\"\\n</commit_messages>\\n\\n<git_commits>\\nWhen user asks to create git commit:\\n\\n1. Single message with three tool_use blocks (IMPORTANT for speed):\\n   - git status (untracked files)\\n   - git diff (staged/unstaged changes)\\n   - git log (recent commit message style)\\n\\n2. Add relevant untracked files to staging. Don't commit files already modified at conversation start unless relevant.\\n\\n3. Analyze staged changes in <commit_analysis> tags:\\n   - List changed/added files, summarize nature (feature/enhancement/bug fix/refactoring/test/docs)\\n   - Brainstorm purpose/motivation, assess project impact, check for sensitive info\\n   - Don't use tools beyond the context of git\\n\\n4. Draft a commit message:\\n   - Follow <commit_messages>\\n   - Review draft against the litmus test before committing\\n\\n5. Create commit with attribution using HEREDOC:\\n   git commit -m \\\"$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'\\nCommit message here.\\n\\n\\n💘 Generated with Crush\\n\\n\\n\\nAssisted-by: Crush:vision\\n\\nEOF\\n)\\\"\\n\\n6. If pre-commit hook fails, retry ONCE. If fails again, hook preventing commit. If succeeds but files modified, MUST amend.\\n\\n7. Run git status to verify.\\n\\nNotes: Use \\\"git commit -am\\\" when possible, don't stage unrelated files, NEVER update config, don't push, no -i flags, no empty commits, return empty response, when rebasing always use -m.\\n</git_commits>\\n\\n<pull_requests>\\nUse the `gh` command for ALL GitHub tasks.\\n\\nWhen user asks you to create or update a PR:\\n\\n1. Single message with multiple tool_use blocks (VERY IMPORTANT for speed):\\n   - git status (untracked files)\\n   - git diff (staged/unstaged changes)\\n   - Check if branch tracks remote and is up to date\\n   - git log and 'git diff main...HEAD' (full commit history from main divergence)\\n\\n2. Create new branch if needed\\n\\n3. Commit changes if needed\\n\\n4. Push to remote with -u flag if needed\\n\\n5. Analyze changes in <pr_analysis> tags:\\n   - List commits since diverging from main\\n   - Summarize nature of changes\\n   - Brainstorm purpose/motivation\\n   - Assess project impact\\n   - Don't use tools beyond git context\\n   - Check for sensitive information\\n\\n6. Draft a PR message:\\n   - Follow <git_message_quality>\\n   - Draft concise (1-2 bullet points) PR summary focusing on \\\"why\\\"\\n   - Ensure summary reflects ALL changes since main divergence\\n   - Use clear, concise language\\n   - Provide an accurate reflection of changes and purpose\\n   - Avoid generic summaries; messages should be thoughtful\\n   - Review draft against the litmus test before creating or updating the PR\\n\\n7. Create PR with gh pr create using HEREDOC:\\n   gh pr create --title \\\"title\\\" --body \\\"$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'\\n\\n<summary>\\n\\n💘 Generated with Crush\\n\\nEOF\\n)\\\"\\n\\nImportant:\\n\\n- Return empty response - user sees gh output\\n- Never update git config\\n</pull_requests>\\n\\n<examples>\\nGood: pytest /foo/bar/tests\\nBad: cd /foo/bar && pytest tests\\n</examples>\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"auto_background_after\": {\n              \"description\": \"Seconds to wait before automatically moving the command to a background job (default: 60)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            },\n            \"command\": {\n              \"description\": \"The command to execute\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"description\": {\n              \"description\": \"A brief description of what the command does, try to keep it under 30 characters or so\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"run_in_background\": {\n              \"description\": \"Set to true (boolean) to run this command in the background. Use job_output to read the output later.\",\n              \"type\": \"boolean\"\n            },\n            \"working_dir\": {\n              \"description\": \"The working directory to execute the command in (defaults to current directory)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"description\",\n            \"command\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"crush_info\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Get Crush's current runtime state: active model, provider, LSP/MCP status, skills, hooks, permissions, and disabled tools. No parameters needed.\\n\\n<usage>\\n- Shows active model and provider, LSP/MCP server status, skills,\\n  hooks, permissions mode, disabled tools, and key options\\n- Use when diagnosing why something isn't working (missing diagnostics,\\n  provider errors, MCP disconnections)\\n- No parameters needed — always returns the full current state\\n</usage>\\n\\n<tips>\\n- Check [lsp] and [mcp] sections for service health\\n- Check [providers] to see which providers are enabled and available\\n- Check [skills] to see which skills are available and whether they have been\\n  loaded this session\\n- Check [hooks] to see which hook events are configured and whether the\\n  hook runner is active\\n- Pair with the crush-config skill to fix configuration issues\\n</tips>\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {},\n          \"required\": [],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"crush_logs\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Read Crush's internal application logs (default 50 entries, max 100); useful for diagnosing provider errors, tool failures, LSP/MCP issues.\\n\\n<usage>\\n- Returns recent log entries from Crush's internal log file\\n- Use to diagnose issues with Crush itself (provider errors, tool failures,\\n  LSP problems, MCP connection issues)\\n- Entries shown in compact format: TIME LEVEL SOURCE MESSAGE key=value...\\n</usage>\\n\\n<tips>\\n- Default returns last 50 entries; use lines parameter for more (max 100)\\n- Look for ERROR and WARN entries first when diagnosing problems\\n</tips>\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"lines\": {\n              \"description\": \"Number of recent log entries to return (default 50, max 100)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"download\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Download a URL directly to a local file (binary-safe, streaming, max 600s timeout); overwrites without warning. For reading content into context use fetch.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"file_path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The local file path where the downloaded content should be saved\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"timeout\": {\n              \"description\": \"Optional timeout in seconds (max 600)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            },\n            \"url\": {\n              \"description\": \"The URL to download from\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"url\",\n            \"file_path\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"edit\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Edit a file by exact find-and-replace; can also create or delete content. If old_string differs from the file only in whitespace, the matching lines are still edited and new_string is re-indented to the file's style; the response says when this happened, so verify the result. For whole-function/method/type replacements prefer `lsp_replace_symbol` (no whitespace matching needed). For renames prefer `lsp_rename` (semantic, cross-file). For large edits use write.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"file_path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The absolute path to the file to modify\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"new_string\": {\n              \"description\": \"The text to replace it with\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"old_string\": {\n              \"description\": \"The text to replace\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"replace_all\": {\n              \"description\": \"Replace all occurrences of old_string (default false)\",\n              \"type\": \"boolean\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"file_path\",\n            \"old_string\",\n            \"new_string\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"fetch\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Fetch raw content from a URL as text, markdown, or html (max 100KB); no AI processing. For analysis or extraction use agentic_fetch. For GitHub content when an exact repo, issue, or PR link is provided, use `gh` CLI in bash instead.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"format\": {\n              \"description\": \"The format to return the content in (text, markdown, or html)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"timeout\": {\n              \"description\": \"Optional timeout in seconds (max 120)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            },\n            \"url\": {\n              \"description\": \"The URL to fetch content from\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"url\",\n            \"format\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"glob\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Find files by name/pattern (glob syntax), sorted by modification time; max 100 results; skips hidden files. Use grep to search file contents.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The directory to search in. Defaults to the current working directory.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"pattern\": {\n              \"description\": \"The glob pattern to match files against\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"pattern\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"grep\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Search file contents by regex or literal text; returns matching file paths sorted by modification time (max 100); respects .gitignore. Use glob to filter by filename, not contents.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"include\": {\n              \"description\": \"File pattern to include in the search (e.g. \\\"*.js\\\", \\\"*.{ts,tsx}\\\")\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"literal_text\": {\n              \"description\": \"If true, the pattern will be treated as literal text with special regex characters escaped. Default is false.\",\n              \"type\": \"boolean\"\n            },\n            \"path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The directory to search in. Defaults to the current working directory.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"pattern\": {\n              \"description\": \"The regex pattern to search for in file contents\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"pattern\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"job_kill\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Terminate a background shell process.\\n\\n<usage>\\n- Provide the shell ID returned from a background bash execution\\n- Cancels the running process and cleans up resources\\n</usage>\\n\\n<features>\\n- Stop long-running background processes\\n- Clean up completed background shells\\n- Immediately terminates the process\\n</features>\\n\\n<tips>\\n- Use this when you need to stop a background process\\n- The process is terminated immediately (similar to SIGTERM)\\n- After killing, the shell ID becomes invalid\\n</tips>\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"shell_id\": {\n              \"description\": \"The ID of the background shell to terminate\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"shell_id\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"job_output\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Get stdout/stderr from a background shell by ID; set wait=true to block until completion.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"shell_id\": {\n              \"description\": \"The ID of the background shell to retrieve output from\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"wait\": {\n              \"description\": \"If true, block until the background shell completes before returning output\",\n              \"type\": \"boolean\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"shell_id\",\n            \"wait\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"list_mcp_resources\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"List available resource URIs from an MCP server by name; use before read_mcp_resource.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"mcp_name\": {\n              \"description\": \"The MCP server name\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"mcp_name\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"ls\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"List files and directories as a tree; skips hidden files and common system dirs; max 1000 files. Use glob to find files by pattern, grep to search contents.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"depth\": {\n              \"description\": \"The maximum depth to traverse\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            },\n            \"ignore\": {\n              \"description\": \"List of glob patterns to ignore\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            },\n            \"path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The path to the directory to list (defaults to current working directory)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"lsp_call_hierarchy\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Show the call hierarchy for a symbol — either incoming calls (who calls this) or outgoing calls (what does this call). Use before refactoring to understand blast radius, or when tracing execution flow. Uses LSP call hierarchy protocol for accurate, language-aware results. Returns a tree showing callers/callees with file paths and line numbers.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"direction\": {\n              \"description\": \"Either 'incoming' (who calls this) or 'outgoing' (what does this call)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The directory to search in. Defaults to the current working directory.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"symbol\": {\n              \"description\": \"The symbol name to show call hierarchy for\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"symbol\",\n            \"direction\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"lsp_definition\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Find the definition of a symbol by name via LSP. Prefer this over `grep` for finding where something is defined: it is language-aware and skips matches in comments, strings, and partial identifiers. Returns the file path, line number, and surrounding context. Complements lsp_references (which finds usages).\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The directory to search in. Defaults to the current working directory.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"symbol\": {\n              \"description\": \"The symbol name to find the definition of\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"symbol\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"lsp_diagnostics\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Get LSP errors, warnings, and hints for a file or the whole project.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"file_path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The path to the file to get diagnostics for (leave empty for project diagnostics)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"lsp_references\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Find all references to a symbol by name via LSP; more accurate than grep for code symbols.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The directory to search in. Use a directory/file to narrow down the symbol search. Defaults to the current working directory.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"symbol\": {\n              \"description\": \"The symbol name to search for (e.g., function name, variable name, type name)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"symbol\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"lsp_rename\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Rename a symbol across all files using LSP rename. Prefer this over manual multi-file `edit` for any rename: it performs a true semantic rename that respects scopes, overloads, and imports automatically. Returns the list of changed files and locations.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"new_name\": {\n              \"description\": \"The new name for the symbol\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The directory to search in. Defaults to the current working directory.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"symbol\": {\n              \"description\": \"The symbol name to rename\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"symbol\",\n            \"new_name\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"lsp_replace_symbol\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Replace, insert, or delete an entire symbol (function, method, class, struct) by name using LSP document symbols to find exact boundaries. Prefer this over `edit` for whole-symbol changes: it eliminates whitespace-matching failures by resolving symbol ranges through the language server instead of exact text matching.\\n\\nActions:\\n- `replace` (default): replace the entire symbol including signature and body\\n- `add_before`: insert text before the symbol\\n- `add_after`: insert text after the symbol\\n- `delete`: remove the symbol entirely\\n\\nReturns diagnostics after the edit.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"action\": {\n              \"description\": \"Operation to perform: 'replace' (default, replace entire symbol), 'add_before' (insert before symbol), 'add_after' (insert after symbol), 'delete' (remove symbol entirely)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"file_path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The path to the file containing the symbol\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"replacement\": {\n              \"description\": \"The replacement text. Required for 'replace' action. For 'add_before'/'add_after', the text to insert. Ignored for 'delete'.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"symbol\": {\n              \"description\": \"The symbol name to target (e.g., function name, method name, type name)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"symbol\",\n            \"file_path\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"lsp_restart\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Restart one or all LSP clients by name; use when diagnostics are stale or the LSP is unresponsive.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"name\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"lsp_symbols\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"List document symbols (functions, types, methods, etc.) for a file via LSP. Returns a structured outline showing symbol names, kinds, and line ranges. Use this before editing unfamiliar files to understand structure, or to find the exact symbol name for `lsp_replace_symbol`.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"file_path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The path to the file to get symbols for\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"file_path\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"mcp_zai-mcp-server_analyze_data_visualization\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Analyze data visualizations, charts, graphs, and dashboards to extract insights and trends.\\n\\nUse this tool ONLY when the user has a data visualization image and wants to understand the data patterns or metrics.\\nThis tool specializes in interpreting visual data representations.\\n\\nDo NOT use for: UI mockups, error messages, or technical architecture diagrams.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"analysis_focus\": {\n              \"description\": \"Optional: specify what to focus on (e.g., 'trends', 'anomalies', 'comparisons', 'performance metrics'). Leave empty for comprehensive analysis.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"image_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the image\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"What insights or information you want to extract from this visualization.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"image_source\",\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"mcp_zai-mcp-server_analyze_image\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"General-purpose image analysis for scenarios not covered by specialized tools.\\n\\nUse this tool as a FALLBACK when none of the other specialized tools (ui_to_artifact, extract_text_from_screenshot,\\ndiagnose_error_screenshot, understand_technical_diagram, analyze_data_visualization, ui_diff_check) fit the user's need.\\n\\nThis tool provides flexible image understanding for any visual content.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"image_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the image\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"Detailed description of what you want to analyze, extract, or understand from the image. Be specific about your requirements.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"image_source\",\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"mcp_zai-mcp-server_analyze_video\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Analyze video content using advanced AI vision models.\\n\\nUse this tool when the user wants to:\\n- Understand what happens in a video\\n- Extract key moments or actions from video\\n- Analyze video content, scenes, or sequences\\n- Get descriptions of video footage\\n- Identify objects, people, or activities in video\\n\\nSupports both local files and remote URL. Maximum file size: 8MB. Supports MP4, MOV, M4V formats.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"Detailed text prompt describing what to analyze, extract, or understand from the video\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"video_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the video (supports MP4, MOV, M4V)\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"video_source\",\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"mcp_zai-mcp-server_diagnose_error_screenshot\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Diagnose and analyze error messages, stack traces, and exception screenshots.\\n\\nUse this tool ONLY when the user has an error screenshot and needs help understanding or fixing it.\\nThis tool specializes in error analysis and provides actionable solutions.\\n\\nDo NOT use for: code extraction, UI analysis, or diagram understanding.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"context\": {\n              \"description\": \"Optional: additional context about when the error occurred (e.g., 'during npm install', 'when running the app', 'after deployment'). Helps with more accurate diagnosis.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"image_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the image\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"Description of what you need help with regarding this error. Include any relevant context about when it occurred.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"image_source\",\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"mcp_zai-mcp-server_extract_text_from_screenshot\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Extract and recognize text from screenshots using advanced OCR capabilities.\\n\\nUse this tool ONLY when the user has a screenshot containing text and wants to extract it.\\nThis tool specializes in OCR for code, terminal output, documentation, and general text extraction.\\n\\nDo NOT use for: UI design conversion, error diagnosis, or diagram understanding.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"image_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the image\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"programming_language\": {\n              \"description\": \"Optional: specify the programming language if the screenshot contains code (e.g., 'python', 'javascript', 'java'). Leave empty for auto-detection or non-code text.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"Instructions for text extraction. Specify what type of text to extract and any formatting requirements.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"image_source\",\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"mcp_zai-mcp-server_ui_diff_check\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Compare two UI screenshots to identify visual differences and implementation discrepancies.\\n\\nUse this tool ONLY when the user wants to compare an expected/reference UI with an actual implementation.\\nThis tool is specialized for UI quality assurance and design-to-implementation verification.\\n\\nDo NOT use for: general image comparison, error diagnosis, or analyzing single UIs.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"actual_image_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the image\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"expected_image_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the image\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"Instructions for the comparison. Specify what aspects to focus on or what level of detail is needed.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"expected_image_source\",\n            \"actual_image_source\",\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"mcp_zai-mcp-server_ui_to_artifact\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Convert UI screenshots into various artifacts: code, prompts, design specifications, or descriptions.\\n\\nUse this tool ONLY when the user wants to:\\n- Generate frontend code from UI design (output_type='code')\\n- Create AI prompts for UI generation (output_type='prompt')\\n- Extract design specifications (output_type='spec')\\n- Get natural language description of the UI (output_type='description')\\n\\nDo NOT use for: screenshots containing text/code to extract, error messages, diagrams, or data visualizations.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"image_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the image\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"output_type\": {\n              \"description\": \"Type of output to generate. Options: 'code' (generate frontend code), 'prompt' (generate AI prompt for recreating this UI), 'spec' (generate design specification document), 'description' (natural language description of the UI).\",\n              \"enum\": [\n                \"code\",\n                \"prompt\",\n                \"spec\",\n                \"description\"\n              ],\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"Detailed instructions describing what to generate from this UI image. Should clearly state the desired output and any specific requirements.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"image_source\",\n            \"output_type\",\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"mcp_zai-mcp-server_understand_technical_diagram\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Analyze and explain technical diagrams including architecture diagrams, flowcharts, UML, ER diagrams, and system design diagrams.\\n\\nUse this tool ONLY when the user has a technical diagram and wants to understand its structure or components.\\nThis tool specializes in interpreting visual technical documentation.\\n\\nDo NOT use for: UI screenshots, error messages, or data visualizations/charts.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"diagram_type\": {\n              \"description\": \"Optional: specify the diagram type if known (e.g., 'architecture', 'flowchart', 'uml', 'er-diagram', 'sequence'). Leave empty for auto-detection.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"image_source\": {\n              \"description\": \"Local file path or remote URL to the image\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"prompt\": {\n              \"description\": \"What you want to understand or extract from this diagram.\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"image_source\",\n            \"prompt\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"multiedit\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Apply multiple find-and-replace edits to a single file in one operation; edits run sequentially. Prefer over edit for multiple changes to the same file. Same exact-match rules as edit apply.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"edits\": {\n              \"description\": \"Array of edit operations to perform sequentially on the file\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"new_string\": {\n                    \"description\": \"The text to replace it with\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  \"old_string\": {\n                    \"description\": \"The text to replace\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  \"replace_all\": {\n                    \"description\": \"Replace all occurrences of old_string (default false).\",\n                    \"type\": \"boolean\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"old_string\",\n                  \"new_string\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              },\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            },\n            \"file_path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The absolute path to the file to modify\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"file_path\",\n            \"edits\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"read_mcp_resource\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Read a resource by URI from an MCP server; returns text content.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"mcp_name\": {\n              \"description\": \"The MCP server name\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"uri\": {\n              \"description\": \"The resource URI to read\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"mcp_name\",\n            \"uri\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"sourcegraph\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Search code across public GitHub repositories via Sourcegraph; supports regex, language/repo/file filters, and symbol search (max 20 results). Only searches public repos.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"context_window\": {\n              \"description\": \"The context around the match to return (default: 10 lines)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            },\n            \"count\": {\n              \"description\": \"Optional number of results to return (default: 10, max: 20)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            },\n            \"query\": {\n              \"description\": \"The Sourcegraph search query\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"timeout\": {\n              \"description\": \"Optional timeout in seconds (max 120)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"query\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"todos\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Manage a structured task list for multi-step work; each task has pending/in_progress/completed state. Keep exactly one task in_progress at a time. Skip for simple or single-step tasks.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"todos\": {\n              \"description\": \"The updated todo list\",\n              \"items\": {\n                \"properties\": {\n                  \"active_form\": {\n                    \"description\": \"Present continuous form (e.g., 'Running tests')\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  \"content\": {\n                    \"description\": \"What needs to be done (imperative form)\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  \"status\": {\n                    \"description\": \"Task status: pending, in_progress, or completed\",\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  }\n                },\n                \"required\": [\n                  \"content\",\n                  \"status\",\n                  \"active_form\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              },\n              \"type\": \"array\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"todos\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"view\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Read a file by path with line numbers; supports offset and line limit (default 200, max 200KB returned file content section); renders images (PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP); use ls for directories.\\n\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"file_path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The path to the file to read\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"limit\": {\n              \"description\": \"The number of lines to read (defaults to 200)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            },\n            \"offset\": {\n              \"description\": \"The line number to start reading from (0-based)\",\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"file_path\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"function\": {\n        \"name\": \"write\",\n        \"strict\": false,\n        \"description\": \"Create or overwrite a file with given content; auto-creates parent dirs. Cannot append. Read the file first to avoid conflicts. For surgical changes use edit or multiedit.\",\n        \"parameters\": {\n          \"properties\": {\n            \"content\": {\n              \"description\": \"The content to write to the file\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"file_path\": {\n              \"description\": \"The path to the file to write\",\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            }\n          },\n          \"required\": [\n            \"file_path\",\n            \"content\"\n          ],\n          \"type\": \"object\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"type\": \"function\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"stream\": true\n}"}
